{% comment %}
  Homepage Instagram row — the Custom Liquid section under "FOLLOW US ON INSTAGRAM".

  The whole widget (profile header, hero, scrolling tiles, hover state, post
  popup) is served from Carbon at /instagram/widget, so this section is just a
  mount point. That keeps the live site and the studio at
  /studio/instagram-widget rendering from one implementation instead of two
  copies that drift apart.

  Posts come from Carbon's own endpoint, which calls Meta at most once every 15
  minutes and serves every shopper from cache — traffic can never exhaust a
  quota, which is what took the previous third-party widget offline. The access
  token stays on the server and never reaches the browser.

  If the feed is ever unavailable the widget renders nothing at all, leaving
  this container empty rather than showing a broken or half-filled section.

  data-hero      the banner image (Shopify Files URL)
  data-hero-text the overlay text on the banner
  data-limit     how many posts to load
{% endcomment %}

<div
  data-carbon-instagram
  data-handle="shopcarbon"
  data-hero="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0680/6572/2620/files/DZ__3128.jpg?v=1733764412"
  data-hero-text="@shopcarbon"
  data-limit="12"
></div>
<script src="https://app.shopcarbon.com/instagram/widget" defer></script>
